"Fee Schedule for July 2026  - 7.7.26 Update (https://kalshi.com/docs/kalshi-fee-schedule.pdf)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 12; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://kalshi.com/docs/kalshi-fee-schedule.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 378\nL0@P1: Trading Fees\nL1@P1: The following terms apply to all event contract markets on the exchange, apart from specific products listed below,\nL2@P1: which have their own fee schedule.\nL3@P1: Trading fees are only charged for orders that are immediately matched with orders sitting on the orderbook. Trading\nL4@P1: fees are not charged for orders placed that are not immediately matched and are instead left as resting orders on the\nL5@P1: orderbook unless they are included in our “Maker Fees” section.\nL6@P1: Trading fees are charged as a variable percentage fee of the expected earnings on an individual contract, which is\nL7@P1: calculated by multiplying the maximum potential earnings from the contract by the implied probability of making those\nL8@P1: earnings, or the price of the contract divided by $1. The current general fee charged for a trade in dollars is given by the\nL9@P1: following formula:\nL10@P1: fees = round up(M x 0.07 x C x P x (1-P))\nL11@P1: P = the price of a contract in dollars (50 cents is 0.5)\nL12@P1: C = the number of contracts being traded\nL13@P1: M = the multiplier for each contract (default is 1 unless otherwise indicated)\nL14@P1: round up = rounds up such that the fee + positionCost is rounded to a centicent\nL15@P1: Maker Fees\nL16@P1: fees = round up(M x 0.0175 x C x P x (1-P))\nL17@P1: P = the price of a contract in dollars (50 cents is 0.5)\nL18@P1: C = the number of contracts being traded\nL19@P1: M = the multiplier for each contract (default is 0 unless otherwise indicated)\nL20@P1: round up = rounds up such that the fee + positionCost is rounded to a centicent\nL21@P1: Please refer to https://kalshi.com/fee-schedule for scheduled upcoming fee changes.\nL22@P1: Maker fees are charged for orders placed that are not immediately matched and are instead left as resting orders on\nL23@P1: the orderbook. These fees are only charged when a trade is ultimately executed, there are no fees associated with\nL24@P1: canceling a resting order.\nL25@P1-2: Last updated and effective: July 7, 2026Settlement Fees\nL26@P2: There is no settlement fee.\nL27@P2: Membership Fees\nL28@P2: There is no membership fee.\nL29@P2: ACH Deposit and Withdrawal Fees\nL30@P2: There is no fee associated with ACH deposits from your bank account to your Kalshi account. There is no fee associated\nL31@P2: with ACH withdrawals to your bank account from your Kalshi account.\nL32@P2: Wire Deposit and Withdrawal Fees\nL33@P2: Fees for wire transfers vary from bank to bank. Kalshi does not charge any additional fees for wire deposit transfers.\nL34@P2: (Withdrawals by wire are not currently supported for transactions under $500,000).\nL35@P2: Debit Deposit and Withdrawal Fees\nL36@P2: Kalshi charges a maximum fee of 2% on card deposits, which may be reduced from time to time based upon standards\nL37@P2: applied fairly and uniformly across members.\nL38@P2: Crypto Deposit and Withdrawal Fees\nL39@P2: Crypto deposits and withdrawals may have associated fees charged by Kalshi’s third-party payment processor. Such fees\nL40@P2: will be clearly disclosed prior to any associated transaction.\nL41@P2: Alternate Payment Method Deposit and Withdrawal Fees\nL42@P2: Kalshi reserves the right to charge between 0% and 2% fees on all rails, and the right to change those rates at our\nL43@P2: discretion.\nL44@P2: Futures Commission Merchant Customers\nL45@P2: Users accessing Kalshi via a third-party Futures Commission Merchant may be charged fees by their Futures Commission\nL46@P2: Merchant that vary from the above fee schedule. Such fees will be disclosed prior to any associated transaction.\nL47@P2-3: Last updated and effective: July 7